                <pb facs="0625" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.6511/154: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-26T18:00:00-04:00">September 26, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>320. The Department’s 319, September 25, 7 p.m. Jones and Guinle signed, at 3:30
                    p.m. today, the exchange of letters on the steel project and the texts as cabled
                    to you yesterday were immediately released to the press.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
